# New in XPPAUT 8.1: sub/supercritical Hopf curves and GH points in AUTO
# Morris-Lecar (type II).
#
# The cell starts exactly at rest for i=0, so no settling run is needed.
# (If you changed something: Initialconds -> Go, then Initialconds -> Last a
#  few times, so it sits exactly on the rest state again.)
#
# 1. File -> Auto. Run -> Steady state.
#    The rest state loses stability at a Hopf point (HB) near i = 102 and
#    regains it near i = 235. With phi = 0.04 both are SUBCRITICAL.
#
# 2. Grab -> Tab to the first HB point (label 2) -> Enter.
#    Axes -> Two par: Main Parm i, 2nd Parm phi,
#       Xmin 80, Ymin 0, Xmax 260, Ymax 0.4   -> Ok.
#    Run -> Two param. (Or keep the axes and use Axes -> Fit afterwards.)
#    AUTO follows the Hopf curve in the (i, phi) plane. It is a closed loop
#    (top near phi = 0.33). New in 8.1:
#      - parts where the Hopf is SUBCRITICAL (first Lyapunov coefficient
#        l1 > 0) are drawn in PURPLE; supercritical parts keep the usual
#        Hopf colour;
#      - a dot labelled "GH" marks each generalised Hopf (Bautin) point,
#        where l1 changes sign. Expect two, near
#           i = 134, phi = 0.24   and   i = 204, phi = 0.16.
#    If the run stops early, Grab the last point and Run -> Two param again
#    (or raise Nmax in Numerics).
#
# 3. To see the difference in one-parameter diagrams: Parameters -> phi = 0.3
#    (above the GH points, supercritical), back to rest, and repeat step 1.
#    Then Grab HB -> Run -> Periodic: the orbits start stable (supercritical)
#    instead of unstable (subcritical, as for phi = 0.04).
#
# i and phi are declared first, so AUTO's Par1 = i and Par2 = phi.
param i=0, phi=.04
param vk=-84, vl=-60, vca=120, gk=8, gl=2, gca=4, c=20
param v1=-1.2, v2=18, v3=2, v4=30
#
dv/dt=(i+gl*(vl-v)+gk*w*(vk-v)+gca*minf(v)*(vca-v))/c
dw/dt=lamw(v)*(winf(v)-w)
minf(v)=.5*(1+tanh((v-v1)/v2))
winf(v)=.5*(1+tanh((v-v3)/v4))
lamw(v)=phi*cosh((v-v3)/(2*v4))
#
# the rest state for i=0
v(0)=-60.899
w(0)=0.014873
#
# XPP: phase plane v-w
@ total=500, dt=0.1, bounds=10000, maxstor=20000
@ xp=v, yp=w, xlo=-80, xhi=60, ylo=-0.05, yhi=0.6
#
# AUTO: diagram of v against i, i from 0 to 300
@ autovar=v
@ autoxmin=0, autoxmax=300, autoymin=-80, autoymax=60
@ parmin=-10, parmax=300
@ ntst=50, nmax=2000, npr=50
@ ds=0.1, dsmin=0.001, dsmax=5
@ normmin=0, normmax=1000
done
